n-o-Lore.</li>\n    </ul>\n</section>","overview":"<section class=\"overview\">\n    <h2>What is JoJo&#039;s Bizarre Adventure?</h2>\n    \n    <p>\n        (often shortened to JoJo or abbreviated as JJBA) is a shōnen and later seinen manga written and illustrated by <a href=\"/jojos-bizarre-adventure/hirohiko-araki\" class=\"entity-link\">Hirohiko Araki</a>, and the main subject of this wikia project.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        JoJo was serialized in Weekly Shōnen Jump from 1987 until 2004, when it then transferred to the monthly seinen magazine Ultra Jump, where the story continues.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        The series has over 100 million copies in print, making it one of the in history. Filling over 120 volumes, it is Shueisha&#039;s second longest-running manga series. Publication in English of the earlier parts of the series is ongoing.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        JoJo&#039;s genre spans Action, Adventure, Supernatural, Thriller, Comedy, Tragedy, Mystery, and Horror. It is perhaps most popularly known for its Stand phenomenon; the Stardust Crusaders arc and its characters Dio Brando/DIO and Jotaro Kujo; the expressive rendition of its proud, glamorous personalities; and its hundreds of nominal references to Western popular music.\n    </p>\n    \n    <p class=\"also-known-as\">\n        <strong>Also known as:</strong>\n        JoJo, JJBA, ジョジョの奇妙な冒険.\n    </p>\n\n</section>","word_count":836,"uniqueness_score":"1.0000"},"entity":{"id":"eba1f22d-8c0b-45a9-a6b3-6e6e84f4ed85","name":"JoJo's Bizarre Adventure","slug":"jojos-bizarre-adventure","type":"topic","kind":"topic","type_label":"Topic","short_description":"(often shortened to JoJo or abbreviated as JJBA) is a shōnen and later seinen manga written and illustrated by Hirohiko Araki, and the main subject of this wikia project.","description":"(often shortened to JoJo or abbreviated as JJBA) is a shōnen and later seinen manga written and illustrated by Hirohiko Araki, and the main subject of this wikia project.\n\nJoJo was serialized in Weekly Shōnen Jump from 1987 until 2004, when it then transferred to the monthly seinen magazine Ultra Jump, where the story continues.\n\nThe series has over 100 million copies in print, making it one of the in history. Filling over 120 volumes, it is Shueisha's second longest-running manga series. Publication in English of the earlier parts of the series is ongoing.\n\nJoJo's genre spans Action, Adventure, Supernatural, Thriller, Comedy, Tragedy, Mystery, and Horror. It is perhaps most popularly known for its Stand phenomenon; the Stardust Crusaders arc and its characters Dio Brando/DIO and Jotaro Kujo; the expressive rendition of its proud, glamorous personalities; and its hundreds of nominal references to Western popular music.","evidence":"fiction","universe":"jojos-bizarre-adventure","aliases":["JoJo","JJBA","ジョジョの奇妙な冒険"],"wikipedia_url":null,"image_url":null,"image_source":null,"image_credit":null,"image_license":null,"image_usage":null,"image_alt":null},"connections":[],"rabbit_holes":[],"copyright":{"theme":"jojos-bizarre-adventure","title":"JoJo's Bizarre Adventure is not owned by Ton-o-Lore.","body":"JoJo's Bizarre Adventure, its characters, artwork, logos, and related intellectual property are the property of their respective rights holders, including Hirohiko Araki, Shueisha, David Production, and other credited rights holders. Ton-o-Lore is an independent, unofficial fan and informational project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by those rights holders. Identification logos and thumbnails, when shown, are low-resolution images used under a fair-use rationale for commentary and identification only — not free or redistributable artwork."},"subject":{"id":"jojos-bizarre-adventure","name":"JoJo's Bizarre Adventure","theme":"jojos-bizarre-adventure","path":"/jojos-bizarre-adventure","logo":{"license":"fair_use","usage":"fair_use_identification","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Jojo%27s_Bizar